    Companion: Aling Nena (mother),
    45 years old

    Setting: Emergency Room, Tertiary Hospital, Philippines

    Reason
    for Visit: Fever for 3 days, severe body aches, jaundice, red eyes

    Notes
    from Nurse: Patient is a market worker. Waded through floodwater with an open
    wound on his foot last week. Eyes are bloodshot (conjunctival suffusion). Skin
    has a yellowish tint (jaundice). Weak and barely responsive. Mother is very worried.'
  interactPrompt: {fileID: 582736895}
